                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The combination of bullet hell and fighting game is genuinely pretty cool, and the game clearly has a lot of complexity and depth. This is very much the type of game you could spend hundreds of hours mastering. There's a decent amount of solo content here, most of it fairly arcade-y. The story isn't particularly interesting, but the focus is clearly on the gameplay rather than the narrative. There's also multiplayer, which is probably where most players will spend their time. The biggest downside is that the game can be very overwhelming when you first start out, but that's often the case when picking up a new fighting game.",
